#![no_std]
#![no_main]

//! 物理内存测试（不依赖任何新增内核接口）
//!
//! 思路：物理内存只有 128 MiB（MEMORY_END = 0x8080_0000），
//! 而这里申请 256 MiB 的虚拟空间。
//!   - 若内核是 eager 分配，sbrk/mmap 在申请时就会耗尽物理页，
//!     frame_alloc().unwrap() 直接 panic，内核关机；
//!   - lazy 分配下，申请只修改 vpn_range，立即返回；
//! 再只访问首/中/尾各一页，验证整个区间都能按需映射。
//!
//! 因此「256 MiB 申请成功且只访问 3 页仍能运行」本身就是
//! 「申请不占物理内存、访问才分配」的证据。

#[macro_use]
extern crate user_lib;

use user_lib::{mmap, munmap, sbrk};

const PAGE: usize = 0x1000;
const BIG: usize = 256 * 1024 * 1024; // 256 MiB > 128 MiB 物理内存

fn touch(addr: usize, val: u8) -> u8 {
    unsafe {
        *(addr as *mut u8) = val;
        *(addr as *const u8)
    }
}

#[no_mangle]
pub fn main() -> i32 {
    let mut ok = true;

    // 1) 堆：一次申请 256 MiB
    let base = sbrk(0) as usize;
    let old = sbrk(BIG as i32) as usize;
    if old != base {
        println!("[lazy-mem] FAIL: sbrk return");
        ok = false;
    }
    println!("[lazy-mem] sbrk {} MiB ok (physical RAM is 128 MiB)", BIG / 1024 / 1024);

    // 2) 只访问首/中/尾三页
    let pages = [base, base + BIG / 2, base + BIG - PAGE];
    for &p in pages.iter() {
        let v = touch(p, 0x5A);
        if v != 0x5A {
            println!("[lazy-mem] FAIL: read back at {:#x}", p);
            ok = false;
        }
    }
    println!("[lazy-mem] touched first/middle/last page of the 256 MiB heap");

    // 3) mmap 一段 256 MiB，访问首/尾
    let a = 0x4000_0000usize;
    if mmap(a, BIG, 3) != 0 {
        println!("[lazy-mem] FAIL: mmap 256 MiB");
        ok = false;
    }
    if touch(a, 0x11) != 0x11 || touch(a + BIG - PAGE, 0x22) != 0x22 {
        println!("[lazy-mem] FAIL: mmap read back");
        ok = false;
    }
    println!("[lazy-mem] mmap {} MiB and touched first/last page", BIG / 1024 / 1024);

    // 4) 收缩，回收
    if munmap(a, BIG) != 0 {
        println!("[lazy-mem] FAIL: munmap");
        ok = false;
    }
    sbrk(-(BIG as i32));

    if ok {
        println!("[lazy-mem] all tests passed");
        0
    } else {
        println!("[lazy-mem] FAILED");
        -1
    }
}
```

Wait: `sbrk(BIG as i32)` — BIG = 268435456, fits i32 (max 2.1e9) ✓.

`touch` returns the byte read back; for the first page, writing 0x5A then reading returns 0x5A ✓.

Address 0x4000_0000 (1 GiB) + 256 MiB: is it free? The heap grows to base+256MB ≈ 0x1000_c000 (256 MiB), so 0x4000_0000 is above it, no overlap. User stack ~0xc000. Fine.

But `mmap` len BIG at 0x4000_0000: the user address space (SV39) supports up to 256 GiB low half; fine.

Touching `a + BIG - PAGE` = 0x4FFF_F000 — fine, below TRAP_CONTEXT (0xffff_ffff_ffff_e000).

One concern: the **kernel's `check_available`** for mmap scans areas; fine.

Another: after `sbrk(-(BIG as i32))`, the heap shrinks from base+256MB to base; `shrink_to` iterates over 65536 pages calling `unmap_one` → each `translate` (page-table walk) → 65536 walks, maybe slow (a few ms). Acceptable. But wait: `shrink_to` in `MemorySet` calls `area.shrink_to`, which iterates `VPNRange::new(new_end, old_end)` and `unmap_one` each. For 65536 pages, each `translate` walks 3 levels → ~200k memory accesses → fine (~ms).

Hmm, actually `unmap_one` first does `page_table.translate(vpn)`; for unmapped pages it returns None quickly? It still walks the page table (3 levels). 65536 * 3 = 196k walks; each walk reads PTEs (cached) → fine.

But the test also has `sbrk(BIG)` which creates an area of 65536 pages; `append_to` only changes the range → O(1) ✓.

Note: this test's `sbrk(256MB)` would **fail (panic)** on an eager kernel — which is the point: success proves lazy. But if the user runs this test on the **eager** version (e.g., before implementing lazy), the kernel panics and the whole run dies. That's acceptable for a lazy-specific test; the README/comment says so.

